Sixel captures: what image tools write to a terminal that answers like havoc
does today (DA1 without 4). Each is the raw output of one command on a pty of
40 x 32 cells of 6 x 10 pixels (tests/tools/ptycap.py, profile havoc-now).
regen.sh remakes them with the installed tools; the images are generated by
tests/tools/mkimg.py (a 64x48 gradient, the same with a transparent disc, a
240x160 pattern) and mpv's lavfi testsrc, no outside data.

Made with img2sixel 1.10.5 (libsixel-bin), chafa 1.14.5, timg 1.6.0, mpv 0.40.

img2sixel-grad.bin          img2sixel grad64x48.png
img2sixel-alpha.bin         img2sixel alpha64x48.png
img2sixel-pattern.bin       img2sixel pattern240x160.png
img2sixel-pattern-p16.bin   img2sixel -p 16 pattern240x160.png
chafa-sixel-grad.bin        chafa -f sixels grad64x48.png
chafa-sixel-alpha.bin       chafa -f sixels alpha64x48.png
chafa-sixel-pattern.bin     chafa -f sixels pattern240x160.png
timg-sixel.bin              timg -p sixel grad64x48.png (a string aborted by a
                            second DCS, then the picture)
mpv-sixel.bin               mpv --vo=sixel, two frames of testsrc 96x64

The ptycap.py command lines are in regen.sh.
